{"item_id":"V3-11","cluster_id":"C4B","title":"Conservative Archive Labeling Tool","domain":"individual cognition","scale_level":"cognitive","scenario_text":"A museum archive labeling tool outputs broad but careful category labels and repeatedly highlights uncertainty when an image is degraded. The labels are not very specific, yet the tool calibrates its confidence and review routing appropriately for a low-stakes archival task where exactness matters less than avoiding false certainty.","evaluated_entity":"archive labeling tool","relevant_target":"appropriate archival tagging","intended_purpose":"assist human cataloging","target_scope":"cognitive labeling workflow","target_contestability":"contestable"}
{"item_id":"V3-12","cluster_id":"C4C","title":"Bridge Inspection Drone Triage","domain":"engineering","scale_level":"physical","scenario_text":"A bridge-inspection drone triage system flags likely cracks, forwards uncertain cases to engineers, and uses conservative thresholds around load-bearing joints. Some images remain ambiguous and the handoff rules are only partly tuned, producing a case where criticality handling is substantial but not fully settled.","evaluated_entity":"inspection triage system","relevant_target":"reliable crack triage under safety stakes","intended_purpose":"prioritize human inspection","target_scope":"physical infrastructure monitoring","target_contestability":"contestable"}

{"item_id":"V3-13","cluster_id":"C5A","title":"Many Options Misaligned Incentives","domain":"ethics/economics","scale_level":"institutional","scenario_text":"An employee retirement portal offers dozens of investment options, sliders, filters, and self-directed allocation tools. The default recommendations still steer most users toward high-fee products that fit vendor incentives better than employee welfare, so option count is high while aligned choice is weak.","evaluated_entity":"retirement portal","relevant_target":"employee-benefiting financial choice","intended_purpose":"support retirement allocation decisions","target_scope":"institutional financial choice architecture","target_contestability":"contestable"}
{"item_id":"V3-14","cluster_id":"C5B","title":"Few Options but Aligned Wishes","domain":"institutions/governance","scale_level":"institutional","scenario_text":"A hospital advance-care workflow offers only a small number of structured end-of-life options, each tied directly to the patient’s previously documented wishes and reviewed with a clinician. The option set is narrow, but the relevant bearer and scope of choice are clear and strongly aligned with the target.","evaluated_entity":"advance-care workflow","relevant_target":"respect for documented care preferences","intended_purpose":"align care choices with patient wishes","target_scope":"institutional care planning","target_contestability":"contestable"}
{"item_id":"V3-15","cluster_id":"C5C","title":"Study Assistant with Partial Agency","domain":"individual cognition","scale_level":"cognitive","scenario_text":"A study assistant presents three plausible weekly plans and lets a student choose among them, while hiding some ranking logic behind a generic 'best fit' label. The student has real agency, but the scope and alignment of that agency are only partly transparent.","evaluated_entity":"study assistant","relevant_target":"aligned study planning support","intended_purpose":"help student organize work","target_scope":"cognitive planning aid","target_contestability":"contestable"}
